1
00:00:00,019 --> 00:00:01,580
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,582 --> 00:00:03,022
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,491 --> 00:00:05,204
(Episode 51)

4
00:00:08,005 --> 00:00:09,265
Everything tastes amazing.

5
00:00:09,326 --> 00:00:12,538
Did you make all this just for us?

6
00:00:13,272 --> 00:00:15,841
You never made food like this at home.
What's the occasion?

7
00:00:16,312 --> 00:00:19,474
Sun Kyung prepared everything today,
from morning until now.

8
00:00:19,619 --> 00:00:21,244
I thought she was going to collapse.

9
00:00:22,364 --> 00:00:23,364
Thank you so much.

10
00:00:23,412 --> 00:00:26,385
I'm just grateful you're enjoying it.

11
00:00:27,005 --> 00:00:29,933
Our first meeting was a little awkward...

12
00:00:30,366 --> 00:00:32,405
Please let this meal make up for it.

13
00:00:34,291 --> 00:00:35,291
It's okay.

14
00:00:35,405 --> 00:00:36,771
A happy ending makes everything okay.

15
00:00:36,773 --> 00:00:41,198
You even remembered and apologized again.

16
00:00:48,411 --> 00:00:50,800
Please have some.

17
00:00:51,590 --> 00:00:52,791
Thank you.

18
00:00:54,389 --> 00:00:55,810
Ji Hu is late, isn't he?

19
00:00:56,238 --> 00:00:57,238
Looks like it.

20
00:01:08,925 --> 00:01:11,150
Spicy rice cakes before the bookstore?

21
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,472
- Sure.
- Let's make it extra spicy.

22
00:01:13,685 --> 00:01:14,685
I'd love that.

23
00:01:35,085 --> 00:01:37,329
- You're here.
- Welcome.

24
00:01:38,531 --> 00:01:39,710
- Sit down.
- Have a seat.

25
00:01:46,245 --> 00:01:48,992
- The stew is really good.
- Thank you.

26
00:01:49,165 --> 00:01:50,767
Does Ji Hu like seafood?

27
00:01:51,318 --> 00:01:54,198
He grew up by the sea,

28
00:01:54,251 --> 00:01:55,524
but he doesn't like seafood.

29
00:01:55,651 --> 00:01:57,538
Your family has very different tastes.

30
00:01:57,645 --> 00:01:59,398
Ji Hu is the only one
who doesn't like seafood.

31
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,951
His dad was a Navy admiral.

32
00:02:05,152 --> 00:02:06,751
That's not true. I like it now.

33
00:02:08,778 --> 00:02:10,918
Don't eat so fast.

34
00:02:10,919 --> 00:02:13,279
- Please get him some water.
- Okay.

35
00:02:16,405 --> 00:02:18,013
Eat slowly.

36
00:02:18,015 --> 00:02:19,511
That's right. Take your time.

37
00:02:26,898 --> 00:02:27,898
It's delicious.

38
00:02:30,228 --> 00:02:32,005
Come in.

39
00:02:32,131 --> 00:02:34,205
It's spacious and lovely.

40
00:02:34,366 --> 00:02:35,366
Right?

41
00:02:35,871 --> 00:02:38,418
It's still not as nice
as a four-bedroom place.

42
00:02:39,998 --> 00:02:41,851
At least say something nice about it.

43
00:02:42,425 --> 00:02:43,838
But it's true.

44
00:02:44,172 --> 00:02:46,645
How will you two live here for a year?
It'll feel so cramped.

45
00:02:49,998 --> 00:02:51,138
Please have some fruit.

46
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:53,105
Sun Kyung must have prepared this.

47
00:02:53,522 --> 00:02:54,791
I'll help too.

48
00:02:54,872 --> 00:02:56,609
Take your time looking around.
Let's go together.

49
00:02:58,815 --> 00:02:59,898
How do you feel?

50
00:03:00,612 --> 00:03:01,697
I'm not sure.

51
00:03:02,092 --> 00:03:03,272
I never expected any of this.

52
00:03:04,511 --> 00:03:05,546
I need to use the restroom.

53
00:03:13,078 --> 00:03:14,973
You and Ji Ni work together
at the publishing company, right?

54
00:03:15,505 --> 00:03:18,658
I heard Do Hee worked with you too.
Did something happen?

55
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:19,911
Do Hee quit.

56
00:03:20,584 --> 00:03:22,175
Wasn't she your fiancée?

57
00:03:23,891 --> 00:03:25,818
- We broke up.
- Why...

58
00:03:26,771 --> 00:03:28,345
Is it okay if I ask?

59
00:03:29,605 --> 00:03:31,465
Maybe I'll tell you another time.

60
00:03:33,345 --> 00:03:34,443
I've always wished...

61
00:03:35,372 --> 00:03:37,446
to have three men and three women
in this family.

62
00:03:37,612 --> 00:03:40,075
Now we have three men and two women.

63
00:03:40,691 --> 00:03:43,210
Come visit us often.
Consider this your mom's home.

64
00:03:43,212 --> 00:03:44,212
Right.

65
00:03:44,438 --> 00:03:46,151
Come whenever you want to see your mom.

66
00:03:46,372 --> 00:03:47,511
You don't have to be formal with us.

67
00:03:47,513 --> 00:03:50,113
Let's not rush it.
We should get closer first.

68
00:03:51,087 --> 00:03:52,087
Okay.

69
00:03:53,865 --> 00:03:57,031
I heard you don't like seafood.
Are you feeling sick? Want some medicine?

70
00:03:57,605 --> 00:03:58,617
It's not that bad.

71
00:04:00,730 --> 00:04:02,228
You went to school with my mom, right?

72
00:04:02,598 --> 00:04:04,008
What was my mom like in school?

73
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,120
Was she a real beauty?

74
00:04:05,431 --> 00:04:06,718
Don't be ridiculous.

75
00:04:08,138 --> 00:04:10,798
I don't think we ever met at school.

76
00:04:10,799 --> 00:04:11,991
We were in different classes.

77
00:04:13,217 --> 00:04:15,757
I heard Yeong Ju was very popular
in the school broadcasting club.

78
00:04:17,011 --> 00:04:18,443
Did you bring the school yearbook?

79
00:04:18,568 --> 00:04:20,497
Right, I'll go get it.

80
00:04:20,499 --> 00:04:22,031
Let's take a look. Just a moment.

81
00:04:27,772 --> 00:04:30,669
Who brings a yearbook
when moving in after marriage?

82
00:04:30,742 --> 00:04:32,214
No Yeong Ju!

83
00:04:32,583 --> 00:04:34,662
Look at her. What a beauty.

84
00:04:39,827 --> 00:04:41,196
There she is. I found her right away.

85
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:42,598
Kim Sun Kyung... Hold on.

86
00:04:46,105 --> 00:04:47,625
How many people have that name?

87
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,509
I think this is my mom, but...

88
00:04:51,259 --> 00:04:52,818
All old photos look like that.

89
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:55,232
In my high school yearbook...

90
00:04:55,658 --> 00:04:57,570
I look like a starving wartime child.

91
00:04:57,572 --> 00:05:00,561
I'm tired. I should get some rest.

92
00:05:00,563 --> 00:05:01,563
What?

93
00:05:01,582 --> 00:05:02,661
I'm going to my room.

94
00:05:04,191 --> 00:05:05,418
I'm tired too.

95
00:05:09,018 --> 00:05:10,018
Why?

96
00:05:10,762 --> 00:05:12,494
We should get going too.

97
00:05:12,545 --> 00:05:16,015
Okay. Come visit again.

98
00:05:25,545 --> 00:05:27,993
- Yes.
- Is your stomach okay?

99
00:05:28,752 --> 00:05:30,367
- Yes.
- Take this.

100
00:05:30,686 --> 00:05:31,889
- Thank you.
- No problem.

101
00:05:40,438 --> 00:05:41,928
- Thanks.
- Sure.

102
00:05:42,210 --> 00:05:43,734
- Please sit down.
- Okay.

103
00:05:45,311 --> 00:05:46,780
How is it living here?

104
00:05:47,479 --> 00:05:49,026
I'm not sure yet.

105
00:05:49,238 --> 00:05:51,945
Your mom and I are quite different.
I'll need time to adjust.

106
00:05:51,965 --> 00:05:53,993
My mom has a childlike side.

107
00:05:54,084 --> 00:05:55,089
Please be patient with her.

108
00:05:56,063 --> 00:05:57,063
I will.

109
00:05:57,625 --> 00:05:59,991
But you really don't look well.

110
00:06:00,145 --> 00:06:01,764
Your uncle... I mean...

111
00:06:01,918 --> 00:06:04,485
Sa Bin could do some acupuncture for you.

112
00:06:06,045 --> 00:06:08,986
I'll bring you some warm plum tea.

113
00:06:10,593 --> 00:06:11,593
Why?

114
00:06:11,883 --> 00:06:12,883
Don't you like it?

115
00:06:14,071 --> 00:06:16,024
That makes me feel all warm and fuzzy.

116
00:06:16,185 --> 00:06:17,386
Warm and fuzzy?

117
00:06:18,905 --> 00:06:22,005
You really do speak like an artist.

118
00:06:22,832 --> 00:06:25,372
I'm feeling warm and fuzzy too.

119
00:06:28,091 --> 00:06:29,091
Ji Hu...

120
00:06:33,065 --> 00:06:34,065
What are you two doing?

121
00:06:34,715 --> 00:06:35,715
Why are you laughing?

122
00:06:36,345 --> 00:06:37,883
You're laughing about the yearbook, right?

123
00:06:38,624 --> 00:06:40,858
No. Come on, Sun Kyung.

124
00:06:41,392 --> 00:06:44,672
Ji Hu seemed to have an upset stomach,
so I gave him some medicine.

125
00:06:45,865 --> 00:06:47,184
As for you,

126
00:06:47,964 --> 00:06:49,611
focus on your husband.

127
00:06:49,752 --> 00:06:50,914
I'll take care of Ji Hu.

128
00:06:51,842 --> 00:06:52,842
Okay.

129
00:06:58,285 --> 00:06:59,285
Mom.

130
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,605
I'm so upset.

131
00:07:02,692 --> 00:07:05,624
Why are your dad and uncle so clueless?

132
00:07:08,292 --> 00:07:10,212
Don't take it to heart.

133
00:07:11,186 --> 00:07:12,412
Okay.

134
00:07:13,932 --> 00:07:15,605
You really have magic hands.

135
00:07:18,252 --> 00:07:19,656
Don't get closer to Yeong Ju...

136
00:07:20,797 --> 00:07:22,732
than you are to me. Understood?

137
00:07:22,793 --> 00:07:23,998
Mom.

138
00:07:23,999 --> 00:07:26,101
Fine. I know that was childish.

139
00:07:26,891 --> 00:07:29,128
- But I still mean it.
- Okay.

140
00:07:43,811 --> 00:07:45,703
Why are you so late?

141
00:07:46,143 --> 00:07:49,471
Move, you clueless husband.

142
00:07:49,518 --> 00:07:52,019
Why are you calling me clueless?

143
00:07:53,270 --> 00:07:57,158
Why did you bring out that yearbook
and upset Sun Kyung?

144
00:07:57,218 --> 00:07:59,378
Women are very sensitive
about that sort of thing.

145
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:00,798
You're right.

146
00:08:02,295 --> 00:08:04,211
That's why I'm worried about the future.

147
00:08:04,905 --> 00:08:07,998
How can I live with your family
with a husband like you?

148
00:08:08,458 --> 00:08:13,123
I must have been completely wrong
about you...

149
00:08:15,091 --> 00:08:17,718
I was just talking to myself.

150
00:08:43,265 --> 00:08:44,265
What are you doing?

151
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:46,358
Why are you up?

152
00:08:46,951 --> 00:08:47,971
I came for some water.

153
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:50,991
The seafood was a little salty.

154
00:08:54,298 --> 00:08:55,650
Mom's doing okay, right?

155
00:08:55,925 --> 00:08:58,625
She'd better be. She can't come back.

156
00:08:58,718 --> 00:08:59,962
Her sister-in-law...

157
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:01,816
is getting to you, right?

158
00:09:02,683 --> 00:09:05,211
What do you mean? She's a nice person.

159
00:09:05,738 --> 00:09:06,932
You're so clueless.

160
00:09:07,365 --> 00:09:09,678
You never had to live
at someone else's mercy,

161
00:09:09,845 --> 00:09:11,098
so you're completely oblivious.

162
00:09:11,783 --> 00:09:13,128
She won't even get her own water,

163
00:09:13,130 --> 00:09:15,098
and she makes mom do it.
Doesn't that worry you?

164
00:09:15,565 --> 00:09:17,118
She won't even get her own son food.

165
00:09:17,243 --> 00:09:19,092
She doesn't lift a finger.

166
00:09:19,418 --> 00:09:20,870
That's how it should be.

167
00:09:20,918 --> 00:09:23,016
- She came into the family as the junior.
- Mai...

168
00:09:23,243 --> 00:09:24,672
said it was strange...

169
00:09:24,853 --> 00:09:26,224
how Koreans rank people
as senior and junior.

170
00:09:26,565 --> 00:09:27,672
Now I totally get it.

171
00:09:27,674 --> 00:09:29,632
Enough nonsense. Go inside and sleep.

172
00:09:32,465 --> 00:09:35,085
By the way, what's up with you and Ji Ni?

173
00:09:36,032 --> 00:09:38,741
When she first came here,
you two seemed to be getting close,

174
00:09:38,962 --> 00:09:40,316
but you've been cold to her lately.

175
00:09:41,850 --> 00:09:43,881
I don't know. I'm confused.

176
00:09:45,965 --> 00:09:48,115
You said you've had to read the room.

177
00:09:48,196 --> 00:09:49,196
Why are you confused?

178
00:10:11,565 --> 00:10:13,460
Did you have a good time yesterday?

179
00:10:14,541 --> 00:10:15,541
Yeah.

180
00:10:25,512 --> 00:10:28,958
You know Sa Bin's nephew who works
at the publishing company with you?

181
00:10:29,085 --> 00:10:30,446
I heard he's Do Hee's fiancé.

182
00:10:30,727 --> 00:10:31,952
"Sa Bin's nephew?"

183
00:10:33,016 --> 00:10:34,691
You mean Ji Hu?

184
00:10:35,058 --> 00:10:37,648
- But I heard they broke up.
- Do you know why?

185
00:10:37,716 --> 00:10:40,026
It's between them, so I don't really know.

186
00:10:40,530 --> 00:10:41,958
Did Do Do Hee say something?

187
00:10:42,631 --> 00:10:44,106
She says they broke up because of you.

188
00:10:44,307 --> 00:10:45,380
Me?

189
00:10:47,485 --> 00:10:48,883
That's not true. She's lying.

190
00:10:48,885 --> 00:10:50,234
Even the night I got drunk,

191
00:10:50,428 --> 00:10:52,271
you two were together and helped me.

192
00:10:52,272 --> 00:10:53,592
He's supposed to be her fiancé.

193
00:10:54,232 --> 00:10:56,518
Isn't it strange
that you were with him that late at night?

194
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,745
There were circumstances that night.

195
00:11:01,432 --> 00:11:02,943
Anyway, I don't date.

196
00:11:03,305 --> 00:11:05,345
Everyone around me knows that.

197
00:11:05,725 --> 00:11:08,012
- "You don't date?"
- No, I don't.

198
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,320
Fine.

199
00:11:09,746 --> 00:11:10,883
Have a good day at work.

200
00:11:21,994 --> 00:11:25,994
(The Captain's Library Publishing)

201
00:11:34,424 --> 00:11:37,198
Just like Ji Ni predicted,
they stole our idea.

202
00:11:37,865 --> 00:11:39,018
I thought there was no way.

203
00:11:39,192 --> 00:11:40,861
I know a guy who works at a print shop,

204
00:11:40,863 --> 00:11:43,121
and he said the latest order
from Fairy Story Publishing Company...

205
00:11:43,195 --> 00:11:44,472
was "The Sun and the Moon."

206
00:11:44,672 --> 00:11:46,018
The part where they fight the tiger.

207
00:11:46,798 --> 00:11:48,863
I asked to see it just in case,

208
00:11:49,144 --> 00:11:50,291
and even the illustrations
are almost identical.

209
00:11:50,293 --> 00:11:52,018
It was a good call to back out...

210
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:53,711
when Ji Ni had a bad feeling about it.

211
00:11:54,058 --> 00:11:56,794
Otherwise, we'd have released an old book
as if it were new.

212
00:11:56,796 --> 00:11:59,339
It'd be such a waste
after all the work we've done.

213
00:12:00,692 --> 00:12:03,121
Let's update the idea and start over.

214
00:12:04,055 --> 00:12:05,055
Okay.

215
00:12:18,072 --> 00:12:19,778
Don't mess with our company again.

216
00:12:19,972 --> 00:12:22,345
I'm not the Na Ji Ni
you used to push around anymore.

217
00:12:22,985 --> 00:12:24,785
If you're curious, go ahead and try me.

218
00:12:31,392 --> 00:12:32,392
Are you okay?

219
00:12:35,603 --> 00:12:38,263
I texted Do Do Hee
and told her not to mess with me.

220
00:12:38,351 --> 00:12:39,459
Look at you, standing up for yourself.

221
00:12:40,732 --> 00:12:43,178
She'd worked on "The Sun and the Moon,"
so it must've been easy for her.

222
00:12:43,285 --> 00:12:46,305
Now she's even going around saying
things to people close to me.

223
00:12:46,512 --> 00:12:48,512
You mean director Cha?

224
00:12:49,577 --> 00:12:51,998
- How did you know?
- I saw him at the shoot that day.

225
00:12:52,872 --> 00:12:55,765
She did the same thing she did to me,
hiding behind the director.

226
00:12:56,298 --> 00:12:58,136
And when the director came
to my home yesterday,

227
00:12:58,138 --> 00:12:59,345
he subtly asked me about it.

228
00:13:00,166 --> 00:13:01,278
I figured he would.

229
00:13:01,825 --> 00:13:04,271
He's your second older brother, right?

230
00:13:05,109 --> 00:13:07,945
I've never really
thought of him as my brother.

231
00:13:08,258 --> 00:13:09,691
He hated me too much.

232
00:13:10,672 --> 00:13:12,924
He even said I never should've been born.

233
00:13:13,351 --> 00:13:14,351
He went that far?

234
00:13:14,438 --> 00:13:16,198
My parents loved each other so much...

235
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:19,200
that everyone else ended up resenting it.

236
00:13:19,678 --> 00:13:22,109
We got a little closer
after the O Reum incident,

237
00:13:22,763 --> 00:13:25,273
so I hate being misunderstood again
because of Do Do Hee.

238
00:13:26,832 --> 00:13:28,110
Even if he can't be my brother,

239
00:13:28,855 --> 00:13:31,818
I just don't want him to be someone
who curses the fact that I was born.

240
00:13:32,632 --> 00:13:33,852
He won't.

241
00:13:34,645 --> 00:13:37,852
Eventually, he'll see who you really are.

242
00:13:38,266 --> 00:13:40,438
- Just like I did.
- What kind of person am I?

243
00:13:42,291 --> 00:13:43,291
A good person?

244
00:13:43,653 --> 00:13:44,672
What?

245
00:13:46,486 --> 00:13:47,486
What are you two doing?

246
00:13:49,332 --> 00:13:50,892
Did you enjoy the spicy rice cakes
yesterday?

247
00:13:51,885 --> 00:13:54,058
Did you two digest them okay without me?

248
00:13:54,698 --> 00:13:56,425
There he is. Sensitive Ji Hu.

249
00:13:56,712 --> 00:13:58,298
I was wondering
why you hadn't fired back yet.

250
00:13:59,165 --> 00:14:00,231
Didn't I tell you?

251
00:14:00,265 --> 00:14:02,065
I knew this guy would never let it go.

252
00:14:02,230 --> 00:14:04,305
How about a team dinner to celebrate
losing "The Sun and the Moon?"

253
00:14:05,152 --> 00:14:06,631
Is that even a thing?

254
00:14:07,205 --> 00:14:09,705
Come to think of it,
we never had a proper team dinner.

255
00:14:12,012 --> 00:14:13,253
You're letting me come too, right?

256
00:14:14,938 --> 00:14:16,998
You really know how to hold a grudge.

257
00:14:19,184 --> 00:14:21,166
You said there were no plans
to publish it at all?

258
00:14:22,863 --> 00:14:24,045
As if.

259
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:27,839
Okay. Got it.

260
00:14:29,845 --> 00:14:30,845
Na Ji Ni,

261
00:14:31,352 --> 00:14:32,938
you think you can dodge my attacks?

262
00:14:34,538 --> 00:14:36,125
You've gotten pretty bold.

263
00:14:42,984 --> 00:14:45,252
There isn't a single photo
of the two of them together.

264
00:14:45,485 --> 00:14:47,606
Na Ji Ni, you're seriously something else.

265
00:14:47,712 --> 00:14:49,025
You've got some tricks up your sleeve.

266
00:14:50,665 --> 00:14:53,087
Why do you keep showing up
at the editing room?

267
00:14:57,365 --> 00:14:59,685
I'm upset because of Ji Ni.

268
00:15:00,532 --> 00:15:01,967
Come on, comfort me.

269
00:15:01,991 --> 00:15:02,991
What about Ji Ni?

270
00:15:03,751 --> 00:15:04,788
Look at this.

271
00:15:04,812 --> 00:15:06,288
"If you're curious, go ahead and try me."

272
00:15:06,290 --> 00:15:08,661
If that's not a threat, then what is?

273
00:15:08,952 --> 00:15:11,322
She stole my boyfriend,
and she has the nerve to say that?

274
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:13,740
Look.

275
00:15:14,545 --> 00:15:17,401
They're always together.
How am I supposed not to suspect them?

276
00:15:20,832 --> 00:15:22,803
She acts so innocent too.

277
00:15:24,299 --> 00:15:27,459
Director, don't let her fool you.

278
00:15:30,801 --> 00:15:31,801
Okay?

279
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:36,916
Thank you.

280
00:15:45,284 --> 00:15:46,543
You're back again.

281
00:15:47,636 --> 00:15:49,191
Why do you keep buying that?

282
00:15:49,613 --> 00:15:51,375
- For your wife?
- Yes.

283
00:15:51,758 --> 00:15:53,507
To get my wife to come back home.

284
00:15:55,170 --> 00:15:56,306
Are you starting a business?

285
00:15:56,831 --> 00:16:00,064
- I'm thinking about it.
- Then let's team up.

286
00:16:00,089 --> 00:16:01,649
With a husband this handsome,

287
00:16:01,674 --> 00:16:04,298
every runaway wife will come back home.

288
00:16:04,979 --> 00:16:06,819
- Take your time choosing.
- Okay.

289
00:16:11,125 --> 00:16:13,508
This way. Be careful.

290
00:16:13,533 --> 00:16:15,412
Watch your step.

291
00:16:21,731 --> 00:16:22,821
What are you doing?

292
00:16:23,276 --> 00:16:25,812
The bed's too small.

293
00:16:25,837 --> 00:16:28,958
Don't let it hit that corner.
Move it to the right. Yeah.

294
00:16:28,982 --> 00:16:30,170
Stop!

295
00:16:34,185 --> 00:16:36,044
What? Still not allowed?

296
00:16:36,072 --> 00:16:37,193
No, you can't.

297
00:16:37,572 --> 00:16:40,092
I told you not to touch anything.
Why do you keep doing this?

298
00:16:40,117 --> 00:16:42,914
- Why do you keep doing this?
- Take it out again.

299
00:16:42,938 --> 00:16:44,932
It can't come in. I'll get a refund.

300
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:49,887
- Come on. Take it out.
- Cha Seung Hyun!

301
00:17:14,172 --> 00:17:16,030
I told you, you can't do that.

302
00:17:17,931 --> 00:17:20,498
If you can't stand the sight of me,
sell the house.

303
00:17:20,959 --> 00:17:22,485
- What?
- You,

304
00:17:22,796 --> 00:17:24,134
when O Reum was sick,

305
00:17:24,289 --> 00:17:26,691
you told me you'd do anything.

306
00:17:26,931 --> 00:17:29,149
So sell the house. We can split the money.

307
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:30,688
Then we'll all be better off.

308
00:17:30,713 --> 00:17:32,056
The house belongs to mom.

309
00:17:32,352 --> 00:17:34,131
It's not my decision to make.

310
00:17:34,452 --> 00:17:36,333
If you want compensation
for O Reum's life,

311
00:17:36,357 --> 00:17:38,310
I'll work and pay you back from now on.

312
00:17:38,532 --> 00:17:39,532
Grandpa...

313
00:17:40,325 --> 00:17:42,109
gave this house to mom.

314
00:17:42,529 --> 00:17:44,852
Because he felt sorry for mom,

315
00:17:45,674 --> 00:17:46,774
who had to live alone because of you.

316
00:17:46,799 --> 00:17:49,041
That was all settled long ago.

317
00:17:49,072 --> 00:17:51,564
Cha Min Ki was punished and died,

318
00:17:51,768 --> 00:17:53,328
and your mom remarried.

319
00:17:53,352 --> 00:17:54,844
The only thing I can offer...

320
00:17:55,721 --> 00:17:56,961
is the annex.

321
00:18:31,038 --> 00:18:32,134
Put it in writing.

322
00:18:32,227 --> 00:18:36,089
If you go against me one more time,
I'll sell this house and leave. Got it?

323
00:18:36,114 --> 00:18:38,148
I told you, this house isn't mine.

324
00:18:38,416 --> 00:18:40,746
You said you'd pay me back
for O Reum's life.

325
00:18:40,771 --> 00:18:42,513
How long is that going to take?

326
00:18:43,152 --> 00:18:44,644
Just write the statement.

327
00:18:47,217 --> 00:18:50,865
So don't lose your temper again.

328
00:18:51,065 --> 00:18:53,444
You think I'm doing this
because I'm any less than you?

329
00:18:53,469 --> 00:18:55,339
When you took my daughter's bone marrow,

330
00:18:55,363 --> 00:18:57,329
do you think I put up with it
because I'm a fool?

331
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:00,133
We're family by blood.
That's why I held back.

332
00:19:00,425 --> 00:19:02,598
Treat Ji Ni well from now on.

333
00:19:03,052 --> 00:19:06,882
No matter how much you reject her,
Ji Ni is still your younger sister.

334
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:48,088
Have you thought about the modeling job
I offered you back then?

335
00:19:53,645 --> 00:19:56,337
You made the right decision. Good.

336
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:58,767
I'm nervous.

337
00:19:58,894 --> 00:20:01,944
- What if I can't do it?
- Don't worry.

338
00:20:02,071 --> 00:20:03,835
It's the age of senior models now.

339
00:20:04,428 --> 00:20:06,267
Let's make this amazing.

340
00:20:06,292 --> 00:20:10,156
I'll find you a modeling academy
and a runway coach.

341
00:20:10,550 --> 00:20:11,550
"An academy?"

342
00:20:12,599 --> 00:20:14,894
I have to learn something else again.

343
00:20:15,004 --> 00:20:17,321
Nothing in life comes easy.

344
00:20:17,322 --> 00:20:18,322
Exactly.

345
00:20:19,263 --> 00:20:21,822
This has to stay a secret
from my daughter.

346
00:20:21,840 --> 00:20:23,669
Yes. Don't worry.

347
00:20:29,092 --> 00:20:31,117
(The Captain's Library Publishing,
Teens Reading Books)

348
00:20:33,429 --> 00:20:35,712
You're worried you'll get photographed
if you're seen with me.

349
00:20:35,723 --> 00:20:37,198
There's no harm in being careful.

350
00:20:37,233 --> 00:20:38,779
I wish you wouldn't worry about that.

351
00:20:40,332 --> 00:20:42,665
We're meeting and talking for work.

352
00:20:42,690 --> 00:20:43,820
Let's not worry about what people think.

353
00:20:45,418 --> 00:20:47,437
I've spent enough of my life
worrying about what others think.

354
00:20:47,790 --> 00:20:48,943
I don't want to anymore.

355
00:20:49,833 --> 00:20:50,833
I understand.

356
00:20:51,432 --> 00:20:53,232
Go downstairs and wait for me.

357
00:20:53,257 --> 00:20:55,004
I need to grab my tablet.

358
00:20:55,028 --> 00:20:56,028
Okay.

359
00:21:42,312 --> 00:21:43,322
Come on in.

360
00:21:43,541 --> 00:21:44,969
There are so many valuable books here.

361
00:21:46,151 --> 00:21:47,151
Really?

362
00:21:50,945 --> 00:21:53,722
This is incredible.

363
00:21:53,746 --> 00:21:56,867
Are all these books
part of your dad's collection?

364
00:21:56,869 --> 00:21:58,794
Some are, and some aren't.

365
00:21:59,559 --> 00:22:02,340
He'd spend months at sea,
so he really loved books.

366
00:22:02,557 --> 00:22:05,116
He must've wanted a lot of them published.

367
00:22:05,865 --> 00:22:07,109
You could say that.

368
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:28,952
You like the storage room, right?

369
00:22:29,638 --> 00:22:31,832
You've really gotten bold.

370
00:22:44,718 --> 00:22:45,718
Hello?

371
00:22:48,078 --> 00:22:49,281
Do Hee.

372
00:22:52,085 --> 00:22:54,472
Looks like you remember
our storage room now.

373
00:22:55,212 --> 00:22:56,674
Go through it again.

374
00:22:57,192 --> 00:23:00,464
Maybe you'll finally realize,
"I really shouldn't have been born."

375
00:23:13,445 --> 00:23:15,127
Ji Ni!

376
00:23:15,511 --> 00:23:17,081
- Ji Ni, are you okay?
- Don't touch me!

377
00:23:22,278 --> 00:23:24,832
Do Hee.

378
00:23:24,856 --> 00:23:25,856
Get me out.

379
00:23:27,018 --> 00:23:29,218
Do Hee, I'm sorry. I was wrong.

380
00:23:29,766 --> 00:23:32,226
- Do Hee.
- Ji Ni!

381
00:23:32,251 --> 00:23:34,671
Ji Ni.

382
00:23:34,673 --> 00:23:35,909
Do Hee.

383
00:23:37,707 --> 00:23:41,243
Dad, please help me.

384
00:23:41,267 --> 00:23:44,053
It's okay, Ji Ni.

385
00:23:44,588 --> 00:23:45,677
Ji Ni!

386
00:23:45,702 --> 00:23:48,054
Ji Ni, breathe. Don't be scared.

387
00:23:48,446 --> 00:23:50,745
Ji Ni, look at me.

388
00:24:23,545 --> 00:24:25,657
Don't be afraid. You're safe.

389
00:24:26,431 --> 00:24:27,647
I'll turn on the light.

390
00:24:29,164 --> 00:24:30,379
There should be a switch here.

391
00:24:39,265 --> 00:24:40,850
I think the switch is outside.

392
00:24:43,124 --> 00:24:44,124
Don't worry.

393
00:24:45,543 --> 00:24:47,768
It's just the two of us now.
You're not alone.

394
00:24:49,783 --> 00:24:51,009
We can get out.

395
00:24:54,797 --> 00:24:56,262
I have my tablet.

396
00:25:02,736 --> 00:25:03,905
You have a messenger app, right?

397
00:25:04,271 --> 00:25:05,271
Yeah.

398
00:25:09,811 --> 00:25:11,094
Do you have Il Dong's contact?

399
00:25:11,871 --> 00:25:12,871
Yes.

400
00:25:23,625 --> 00:25:24,895
He'll be here soon.

401
00:25:27,911 --> 00:25:29,152
I was really scared, right?

402
00:25:29,465 --> 00:25:31,059
My heart broke for you.

403
00:25:32,371 --> 00:25:33,627
You looked so helpless.

404
00:25:34,731 --> 00:25:37,451
Dad saved me.

405
00:25:41,571 --> 00:25:42,638
Dad...

406
00:25:44,058 --> 00:25:45,935
Dad, I miss you.

407
00:25:53,638 --> 00:25:54,792
Wait a moment.

408
00:25:56,729 --> 00:25:57,729
Don't go.

409
00:26:01,111 --> 00:26:02,221
It's okay.

410
00:26:13,052 --> 00:26:14,052
Here!

411
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:16,527
What's this?

412
00:26:16,881 --> 00:26:18,570
The Captain's Bookshop.

413
00:26:18,967 --> 00:26:21,096
It's from my dad's collection.
What do you think?

414
00:26:21,132 --> 00:26:22,227
Do I look like Captain Hook?

415
00:26:24,498 --> 00:26:25,498
Cute.

416
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:28,694
Cute? Don't I look cool?

417
00:26:46,418 --> 00:26:47,455
Are you okay?

418
00:27:03,218 --> 00:27:05,325
Want to go for a run?

419
00:27:05,452 --> 00:27:06,860
To celebrate being free.

420
00:27:07,056 --> 00:27:08,554
"Celebrate being free?"

421
00:27:10,012 --> 00:27:11,012
Sure.

422
00:27:13,978 --> 00:27:15,439
I'm going this way.

423
00:27:17,353 --> 00:27:18,756
Let's go together.

424
00:27:19,309 --> 00:27:20,309
Ji Ni!

425
00:27:24,191 --> 00:27:26,323
Ji Ni, you're a pretty good runner.

426
00:27:27,966 --> 00:27:29,775
Where are you going?

427
00:27:35,975 --> 00:27:37,315
- Over there.
- What's this?

428
00:28:30,472 --> 00:28:33,854
(Family Register)

429
00:28:33,856 --> 00:28:35,419
It looks like
Do Hee still hasn't moved on.

430
00:28:35,443 --> 00:28:36,724
Shouldn't you give her some time?

431
00:28:36,748 --> 00:28:38,320
I think you're the problem.

432
00:28:38,345 --> 00:28:40,745
I'll make Na Ji Ni wish she were dead.

433
00:28:40,770 --> 00:28:43,727
And I'll make you beg me to marry you.

434
00:28:43,752 --> 00:28:46,219
- Have you changed?
- Yes, I have.

435
00:28:46,244 --> 00:28:47,984
You think I don't think about you?

436
00:28:48,009 --> 00:28:49,667
You're so frustrating, Sa Bin!

437
00:28:49,692 --> 00:28:52,198
Come to my house today
and put everyone in their place.

438
00:28:53,741 --> 00:28:55,741
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
